{#- A case study's header, the one place it is written: the title with one line of facts under it, the
    cover with its artefact laid on it, and a small table of the rest. Included by layouts/project.njk, so
    every project has the same header and only its front matter differs.

    Nothing is required except a title. Whatever is missing is left out, never shown empty: a field
    without a value is not drawn, a table with no rows is not drawn, no cover image means no cover.
    The page's description is not shown here (it is for search and share previews): the header does not
    say twice what the title and the facts already say.

    Title block, in a frame on the mat's lines (as in the Figma's pj-header)
      industry          one mono line above the heading
      title, headline   the heading (headline: when it differs from the title the cards and pager use), titleSup

    Cover
      coverImage, coverPosition
      thumbnail + thumbnailKind (phone | print | book) [+ mockupImage for a phone]: the artefact laid on it

    Table: one row each, in this order, for whichever the page has
      client, role, platform, deliverables (shown as "Output"; one value, or a list of two or so)
      facts         any other rows this kind of project needs, in order: [{ label, value }]
                    (a data project might add "Data", "Method", "Tools"; a design project "Research")
      team          the people who did the work with me: [{ name, role?, url?, photo? }]. With a photo for
                    everyone, a row of faces: each shows its name and role under it on hover, focus
                    or a tap, linked to the person's profile (tip.js). Without, a list of names.
                    A photo is the 224px square with its grey ring built in (scripts/team-avatar.js).
    Each row is one line: the label, then the value, so keep a value short. A list value
    (deliverables: [a, b]) is a short bulleted list, a line each.
    The table is centred in its container, which is fixed to the grid: its rows are spread evenly
    through it (snap.js, "facts"). -#}
{%- set rows = [] %}
{%- for pair in [["Client", client], ["Role", role], ["Platform", platform], ["Output", deliverables]] %}
  {%- if pair[1] %}{% set _ = rows.push([pair[0], pair[1]]) %}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for extra in facts %}
  {%- if extra.value %}{% set _ = rows.push([extra.label, extra.value]) %}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{%- if title %}
<header class="sheet title-plate" style="--w: 9; --h: 3" data-snap>
  {%- if industry %}
  <p class="label header__meta">{{ industry }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
  <h1>{{ headline or title }}{% if titleSup %}<sup class="title-sup">{{ titleSup }}</sup>{% endif %}</h1>
</header>
{%- endif %}

{%- if coverImage %}
<figure class="sheet cover" style="--h: 6">
  <div class="frame frame--plain"><img src="{{ coverImage }}" alt="" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 90vw, 880px" loading="eager"{% if coverPosition %} style="object-position: {{ coverPosition }}"{% endif %}></div>
  {%- if thumbnail %}
  {%- if thumbnailKind == 'phone' and mockupImage %}
  <span class="card__art card__art--phone"><span class="phone-frame"><img src="{{ mockupImage }}" alt="" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 30vw, 216px" loading="eager"></span></span>
  {%- else %}
  <span class="card__art card__art--{{ thumbnailKind or 'print' }}"><img src="{{ thumbnail }}" alt="" sizes="220px" loading="eager"></span>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}
</figure>
{%- endif %}

{%- if rows.length or team.length %}
<dl class="sheet facts" style="--x: 6; --w: 7; --h: 3" data-snap>
  {%- for row in rows %}
  <div><dt class="label">{{ row[0] }}</dt><dd>
    {%- if row[1] is string %}{{ row[1] }}{% else %}<ul class="facts__list">{% for item in row[1] %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif -%}
  </dd></div>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if team.length %}
  {%- set faces = true %}
  {%- for member in team %}{% if not member.photo %}{% set faces = false %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  <div><dt class="label">Team</dt><dd>
    {%- if faces %}
    <ul class="faces">
      {%- for member in team %}
      <li class="face" data-tip="hover">
        <{% if member.url %}a href="{{ member.url }}" rel="noopener"{% else %}span tabindex="0"{% endif %} class="face__link" aria-label="{{ member.name }}{% if member.role %}, {{ member.role }}{% endif %}">
          <span class="face__img"><img src="{{ member.photo }}" alt="" width="56" height="56" sizes="56px" loading="eager"></span>
          <span class="tip"><span class="tip__card face__card"><span class="face__name">{{ member.name }}</span>{% if member.role %}<span class="face__role">{{ member.role }}</span>{% endif %}</span></span>
        </{% if member.url %}a{% else %}span{% endif %}>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- else %}
    <ul class="team">
      {%- for member in team %}
      <li>{% if member.url %}<a href="{{ member.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ member.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ member.name }}{% endif %}{% if member.role %} <span class="team__role">{{ member.role }}</span>{% endif %}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- endif %}
  </dd></div>
  {%- endif %}
</dl>
{%- endif %}
